The concrete pile foundation will have a long cylindrical shape, made from sturdy materials such as concrete, reinforced cement, etc. Using concrete and piles of Melaleuca poles to push down acts as a way to support the stability of the material structure.
This type of foundation is widely used in civil and public works. It is even used in large projects such as hydroelectric power plants, solar energy, hospitals, hotels, high-rise buildings, apartments, etc.
Currently, there are two types of concrete pile foundation commonly used: square pile foundation and round pile foundation.
-Higher bearing capacity than round piles with the same cross-section, better concrete quality than round piles with Mac
Disadvantages -The cost is a bit higher than the round pile when produced in the same factory
-Easily broken during construction, especially for piles with large cross-sectional surface
Do not use piles with deviations exceeding regulations and with cracks no more than 0,2 mm wide. The depth of cracks in the corners should not be more than 10 mm.
Dimensions of cross-sectional edge of solid or hollow center pile (mm) +5
Deviation of pile tip from center (mm) 10
Capable of lowering piles to the designed depth with specified rejection, through thick soil layers and including a rigid clamping layer.
The total time to lower the pile or the number of strokes including the total does not exceed the control value in the design to prevent pile fatigue. The rejection of the pile should not be too small because it can easily damage the hammer head.
When vibration lowers the pile in the sand and in the final stage, reduce the frequency and drop the pile between 7 min and 10 min. At design depths, to compact the soil inside and around the pile.
For piles with a diameter of more than 1m, it is recommended to place the scour chimney according to the circumference of the pipe piles, spaced from 1m to 1,5m apart. The scour pipe with the nozzle should be conical, the diameter of which is preferably about 0,4 to 0,45 times the diameter of the scour pipe.
Select the pile equipment that meets the standard conditions. Selecting the reaction system for pile pressing should in no case be less than 1,1 times the maximum pressure specified by the design.
The shaft of the equipment needs to coincide with the center of the pile
Check the top surface of the pile, adjust it to be very smooth, check the details of the joints. Install and erect the pile segment in the pressing position so that the center axis of the pile segment must coincide with the axis of the pile tip, the allowable tilt deviation from the vertical is not more than 1%.
Gradually increase the pressure on the concrete piles that penetrate the soil at a speed not greater than 2 cm/s. The tip of the stake should not be used in hard clay for too long.
