Eccentric foundation is a type of foundation with the feature that the center of the column does not coincide with the center of the foundation calyx. This method of foundation construction is often used in the design and construction of townhouses, built with an unfavorable ground area.
Deviation here is the eccentricity with respect to the foundation calyx. Especially for houses built in a row, the house columns will often have to be close to the boundary of the neighboring house.
For small-scale works, the center of gravity of the column and the center of the tower coincide, the moment of the foot of the column is usually very small. But for the eccentric foundation, the moment is very large, due to the additional work of the torque generated by the eccentricity.
Moment is a mandatory factor to be taken into account in the calculation of the eccentricity. Because it has a direct influence on important nail steps such as the arrangement of the foundation steel.
Option 1 is the case of arranging piles evenly and option 2 is arranging piles close to the boundary. To compare the two cases, for the pile arrangement close to the edge, the pile head load will be more uniform.
One way to reduce eccentricity is to add anti-roll columns. This is also one of the solutions that are applied a lot.
To be able to add anti-roll columns in the propeller foundation in the house, one also needs a specific calculation formula. The resistance to tipping is related to the resistance of the soil at the front and back of the foundation.
