Winter Sales 2022: All about Dates, Private Sales & Good Deals in Guide , Shopping
The 2022 winter sales have started!
The month of January will be conducive to good business with the start of the 2022 winter sales in France.
If you weren't able to find good deals during Black Friday or before the Christmas holidays, you will be able to make up for it in a few days. Indeed, the 2022 winter sales will take place at the beginning of January.
How do sales work?
Indeed, the region located near Luxembourg benefits from an exemption to start sales earlier so as not to be left behind by the neighboring country, which started sales earlier than France.
Therefore, the start and end dates for the digital sale are Wednesday, January 12 through Tuesday, February 8. E-shops accessible online from France, regardless of their head office, must respect the same deadlines and display their limited-time offers on the same sales dates.
They create too much confusion for consumers with little impact on the economy.
The Winter 2022 sales started at the same time throughout France with a few exceptions. These concern overseas departments, where the seasons differ as in France and the border regions of the countries where the dates of the winter sales differ.
ÀSaint Pierre and Miquelon, the 2022 winter sales will take place fromWednesday January 19at 8 a.m. to Tuesday, February 15.
ÀRéunion, the 2022 winter sales will start onSaturday 3 Septemberat 8 a.m. and will end on Friday, September 30.
Private sales are one of the options available to major clothing brands when they wish to destock without selling off their products in their own stores.
Most pre-sales and private sales start a few weeks before the official sales date with interesting promotions.
Once you've received an invitation, usually via email and/or text message from the online store, you should be ready to show up when the sale begins. During a private sale, you can usually see real-time stock levels for each item.
The government abolished this provision, Law No. 626 of 2014 of June 18, 2014, which put an end to the two weeks of floating sales by putting them at the end of the traditional sales, which therefore last 6 weeks instead of 5 weeks.
Sales are governed by the legal texts set out in the Commercial Code. There are two types of sales: national sales and floating sales.
The Commercial Code also provides for certain exemptions for border provinces and overseas territories.
For example, promotional items must have been on sale for at least one month and the original price and promotion must be displayed on the product. During sales, the store must also have a facility to clearly distinguish sale items from other items.
According to a study commissioned by technology company Invibes Advertising, 51% of French people intend to make a purchase during the sales, and 78% of them take advantage of barred prices to buy fashion items. While the best finds are usually made in the first week, the second and third price drops can give you a real bargain to complete your wardrobe without breaking the PEL.
So on your marks, get ready, shop! Also see: Best Reliable and Cheap Chinese Online Shopping Sites & 25 Best Free Sample Sites To Try
Unless there is an exceptional delay, the sales must take place throughout the national territory. between Wednesday June 22, 2022 at 8 a.m. and Tuesday July 19, 2022 in the evening.
