This is a question that often comes up when you move in your living room: how far should you plan between the sofa and the TV?
After all, when you go to the cinema, you carefully choose your place in the room. Well at home, it's the same thing!
Here are four pieces of information:
Note that you will have to adapt these distances if your TV has Blu-ray or if you use video games. The term "small screen" is no longer too valid today.
It is therefore necessary to multiply it by 2 or 3 times, according to preferences, in order to obtain the distance. For example, if your TV is 100 cm diagonal, the correct distance is between 2 and 3 meters.
The distance for 4k TV
You can calculate the ideal setback distance yourself and knowing the dimensions of your TV screen and to obtain it you just need to multiply the size of the screen by 1,2:
Since the arrival of high definition, the pixels are much finer and it is now possible to enjoy your television close to the screen. The calculation is no longer done on the diagonal of the screen, but on its height.
There is therefore no need to have 6 m of distance for your 4-inch 85K TV since, based on these figures, less than 2 meters is enough.
