According to the introduction, osteoclasts are like the termites in the tree, once active, even the towering tree, but also because of long-term decay and fall. Current studies believe that the primary cause of osteoporosis is abnormal activation of osteoclasts, and acid secretion by osteoclasts is considered to be the key initial factor of bone destruction by osteoclasts and the necessary prerequisite for their degradation of bone tissue.
In addition, although osteoclasts are the cause of osteoporosis, many studies have shown that they play a role in promoting bone formation and angiogenesis as “precursor cells” before secreting acid. Therefore, it is very important to accurately inhibit osteoclasts.
Lin Xianfeng, an orthopedic surgeon at Run Run Shaw Hospital of Zhejiang University, said that the study found that alkaline liposome materials and the local acidic environment of osteoclasts induced a large number of apoptosis of osteoclasts, and further released a large number of extracellular vesicles.”It’s like a set of dominoes, which are pushed one layer at a time and magnified one step at a time to fully resist the bone destruction caused by the strengthening of osteoclasts.”
