Galvanised steel angle lintel is a carbon structural steel for construction, which is a section steel with simple section, and is mainly used for metal components and frame of factory buildings, etc. It is a strip of steel with two sides perpendicular to each other and angled.
The allowable range of steel angle bar geometry deviation is also stipulated in the standard, which generally includes items such as bending degree, side width, side thickness, vertex angle, theoretical weight, etc., and it is stipulated that the angle steel shall not have significant torsion.
Galvanised steel angle lintel can be composed into different bearing components with different structures; it can also be used as joint pieces between the components. It’s mainly used in various building structures and engineering structures, such as beams, bridges, transmission towers, lifting and transportation machinery, ships, industrial furnaces, reaction towers, container racks, cable trench supports, power piping, bus support installation, and warehouse shelves.
