Landing pages play a crucial role in lead generation. To stimulate conversions, they must capture the attention of your target audience, build their confidence with the right information, and compel them to take the next step.
If you’re using WordPress, you may notice that the built-in page builder isn’t exactly an ideal tool for landing page creation. But since WordPress is all about flexibility, you can still build a decent landing page through the HTML editor.
In this article, we’ll take a look at five of the best landing page plugins for WordPress, examine their pros and cons, and help you decide which one is best for your website.
Beaver Builder implements a minimalistic interface with a top-to-bottom approach. For example, before adding page elements such as text and images, you can specify a base layout you want to work with.
InstaBuilder 2.0 is a comprehensive tool that allows you to create, launch, and optimize your landing pages. It utilizes a drag-and-drop page builder that can help you add page elements such as buttons, headlines, and copy with ease.
The toolbar animations are fluid and page elements can be adjusted or repositioned using only the mouse. If you need extra formatting options, simply click on any element to show another toolbar as well as a settings panel to the right.
If you want an even faster way to build landing pages, InstaBuilder allows you to use “combos” that comprise of elements that are often used together for better conversions. You can also customize combos to tailor the tool to your specific needs.
Image Editor –To make your images look better, you can simply use the integrated image editor that uses technology from Adobe Aviary SDK. This streamlines and speeds up the process for those who utilize a lot of visual elements.
Advanced Page Features –Aside from the key features mentioned above, InstaBuilder also provides you with a bunch of additional features such as a welcome gate, exit popup, count-down timer, and free pre-made graphics.
Everything can be dragged around, edited, and resized from the main editor. To change the background, hover the page with your mouse and click the blue “Edit” button.
Design Review – To receive design insights from experts, you can submit your landing page for review. You can then either send your page’s URL or capture a screen recording via a browser extension.
Start with “Edit in Live Compose”.
Notice that Live Composer works similarly to Beaver Builder, which also integrates directly with WordPress. This means you’ll be working with the currently installed theme for your website.
Remember that a minor issue with Live Composer’s interface is that you can’t scroll through the menu items normally. Instead, you need to use the left and right buttons to move the menu.
Notable Features: Extensions – The plugin comes with an extension store where you can find free and paid With extensions, you can add functionalities such as Google Maps support, marketing icons, animations, and so on.
New Dashboard Features –After installing Live Composer, new sections will be added to your WordPress dashboard: Testimonials, Downloads, Galleries, Partners, Projects, and These sections are tied to the appropriate module in the editor.
Right off the bat, you can see that Lander has the most modernized interface out of all the plugins mentioned in this list. It loads quickly and responds well – thanks to the minimalistic interface.
Creating and editing your landing page in Lander.
Auto-fill Forms – To improve user experience, the landing pages you create with lander can use the “auto-fill” feature. The app automatically takes data from past forms filled out by the user.
What is the Best Landing Page Plugin for WP?
If you want a plugin that can help you create landing pages and customize existing pages, then you should take a look at Beaver Builder.
Home › Blog › Blogging Tips › Complete Guide to Re-purposing Old Content
Your content is one of your biggest assets as a website owner. You've likely invested a lot of time, effort and money into developing the best content you possibly can for your site and your readers.
One way you can take your content to the next level is by making sure it stays at the forefront and continues to grab attention long after it is initially published. You can do this by re-purposing old content.
You've just spent your time instead of actual money when you do all of the work yourself. It has often been said that “time is money”, so we'll go with these figures.
Now, let's say you find more than one way to re-purpose that same content.
