Usage statistics show that WordPress is the most popular content management system (CMS) today. Powering over 26% of the entire web, it’s clearly a favorite amongst bloggers, web designers, and online entrepreneurs.
Below are thirty of the most downloaded and highly rated plugins you should consider when building and hosting your WordPress website:
WP-PageNavi allows you to customize your WordPress site’s pagination links. It does, however, require you to replace a few bits of code via Appearance > Editor upon setting up.
Contact Form 7 is a simple and flexible plugin that allows you to create quick contact forms using HTML. You can then insert these forms to any page via shortcode.
Yoast SEO is a popular plugin that can help you with on-page optimization. It helps detect issues, generate sitemaps, and provide recommendations that can improve your site’s rankings.
Akismet is another plugin that can help prevent spam. It automatically scans and filters all shady comments for manual review.
The SiteOrigin Page Builder plugin words by adding a drag and drop interface in the page editor. You can build a new page from the ground up or use a pre-built layout to save time.
Regenerate Thumbnails is a handy tool that can recreate all thumbnails for your media uploads. This is useful if you’ve recently changed the thumbnail settings from Settings > Media.
As a failsafe, make sure you have backups that will help you recover from unexpected problems. With UpdraftPlus, you can easily create or schedule automated backups for added security.
With Black Studio TinyMCE Widget, you can easily add rich text, media attachments, and other content elements in sidebars.
Ninja Forms installs a drag and drop form editor into your WordPress installation. It’s a user-friendly plugin that can guide you every step of the way.
With Breadcrumb NavXT, you can provide your visitors with navigational links to help them determine where they are. Once installed, you need to paste a simple ‘div’ code to where you want the “breadcrumb” trail to appear.
WP Mail SMTP allows you to use SMTP and access advanced options for your site’s email function. To use the plugin, go to Settings > Email from your dashboard.
The Events Calendar plugin allows you to create interactive pages for events like promotions, parties, and seminars. Simply use the visual interface to fill in the details and publish your event.
